                <pb facs="0506" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/549: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Agua Prieta</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Douglas, Ariz</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-08T11:00:00-07:00">April 8, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Fighting not yet resumed at Naco. General Topete in conference at this office
                    late Sunday with General Cocheu stated that he had withdrawn troops Saturday
                    because of the fear of causing international complications by bullets falling in
                    American territory. He stated that he will reopen his attack at once. Situation
                    in other parts remain[s] unchanged.</p>
                <p>Claim by Harry Baker, American citizen hurt by rebel bomb at Naco, has been
                    settled by <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> government to his satisfaction.
                    He has been discharged as well from local hospital.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
